# ============================================================================
# What the Docker build context excludes.
#
# Without this the context carries the whole of `apps/web/node_modules` and any
# local `backend/target`, which slows every build and — worse — lets a stale
# artifact from a previous local build sit where the image expects a fresh one.
#
# The image builds the application from source in both stages, so none of this
# is needed to produce it.
# ============================================================================

# --- Dependencies and build output: rebuilt inside the image -----------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
target
**/target
dist
**/dist

# --- Version control and tooling ---------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.playwright-mcp

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never bake a local `.env` into an image: the platform supplies the real values
# as environment variables, and an image that carries a development signing key
# is one that can be pushed somewhere it does not belong.
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# --- Not needed to build -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
docs
dashboard.png
run-application.txt
